release, the Nexus index, is tagged nexus-v<VERSION> and titled Nexus v<VERSION>, where it was tagged nexus and
titled Nexus: nexus-index.yml removes every earlier index and its tag (nexus-v*, and nexus) and makes it again
after each suite release, and now also after a push to main that changes VERSION. tools/check_versions.py checks
that VERSION is x.y.z. The release tags ruleset must exclude nexus-v* (the Nexus page, GitHub settings), or the
workflow cannot remove the old index tag. Every disclaimer looks the same: the BC250 suite's home page ends with the
shared text too (<!-- disclaimer --> in bc250-bazzite/docs/index.md), and tools/tests/test_disclaimer.py asks it of
