Changelog: 28-10-2026 00:12:46

Nexus's shared checks run in a workflow of their own, .github/workflows/ci-nexus.yml (owner, 27-10-2026: first on
the backlog): the versions of core and dev/ (tools/check_versions.py --nexus, new), every CHANGELOG keeping its
entries, the tests of core, tools and dev/releases, bash -n and shellcheck on tools/, test.sh and dev/, the line
endings, the exec bits, the four files of core, dev/* and the root, workflows only at the root, and the Nexus page
built strictly. ci.yml keeps the BC250 Bazzite Suite's checks alone, so a failure in Nexus's is Nexus's and one
suite's checks never hold another suite's tags. Every suite's tags wait for ci-nexus.yml besides the suite's own
CI: tools/tag-release.sh asks tools/ci_state.py about it too, and the ci job of release.yml and
release-windows-portable.yml waits for it after the suite's CI (up to 75 minutes each; both run on the same push).
tools/ci-local.sh runs the jobs of both workflows, ci-nexus.yml's as nexus-<job> (nexus-shell, nexus-pytest/core),
