complete stylesheet with its own --nexus-* variables, so a change in one wiki's design panel or stylesheet reaches
no other. Both wikis look the same as before, pixel for pixel. Both stylesheets begin with labeled groups (the
suite's colors, corners, header, Material's main and hover colors, the page), and the header's background and
text have variables of their own (--suite-header-bg and --suite-header-fg, --nexus-header-bg and --nexus-header-fg):
the header text was a fixed white the panel could not change. The design panel names each group and row by the
stylesheet's comments, shows the variable's name below and where it is used on hover, gives a color picker to a
variable that refers to a color, and names the wiki it changes and the file Copy CSS belongs in.
tools/tests/test_wiki_designs.py checks that no wiki inherits or shares another's files and that every variable is
labeled. The Nexus page's Design chapter describes the groups.

