Changelog: 23-10-2026 04:20:59

The wiki's USB HD Cam chapter says which half of a side-by-side frame is which lens: each half is the lens on that
side as one faces the camera (owner's board, 23-10-2026: with the lens on the left seen from behind covered, the right
half of a 2560x800 frame went dark).
Its picture section lists the frame sizes and which modes give a picture on the BC-250 with Reduced bandwidth,
measured mode by mode (23-10-2026).
It also says why the exposure time cannot be used: asked directly, past uvcvideo (23-10-2026), the camera offers
only Auto and Shutter Priority, flags the exposure time as decided by its automatic exposure in both, takes a value
in Shutter Priority but puts it back to 1000 when a stream starts (2 ms and 30 ms gave the same picture).

Changelog: 23-10-2026 03:50:44

The wiki's USB HD Cam chapter says what to do after a restart: the camera keeps its power and firmware through
a warm restart of the board but does not reconnect (both USB 3 ports "not attached" on the owner's board,
23-10-2026), and switching the ports off and on from Linux (usb7-port*/disable) does not bring it back (no USB
event at all, so most likely the ports' power is not cut), so the camera needs to be unplugged and plugged in again.
After a shutdown and power on it starts fresh and the load service loads it at login (owner's board, 23-10-2026).

