Changelog: 17-10-2026 06:29:57

tools/pin_app.py pins an app whose [apps.<name>] table has no sha256 line yet, as a new app is listed until its
first release: the line is added after the tag line. Before, it stopped with "[apps.<name>] has no sha256 line",
which took BC250 Suite Releases down with it on the owner's Pin of fan-control-v0.1.0 (17-10-2026).

Changelog: 17-10-2026 05:12:58

A new app, BC-250 USB Wi-Fi (apps/usb-wifi, changes_board): the driver for AIC8800D80 USB Wi-Fi sticks, which
Bazzite's kernel lacks, built on the board for the running kernel from pinned sources (shenmintao/aic8800d80, the
branch chosen from the chip's answer in the kernel log) and installed as a system service that loads it at every
boot, switches the stick out of storage mode and rebuilds it after a kernel update. CI runs its tests, its
shellcheck and its installer test (tools/installer-tests/usb-wifi.sh); the Dependency Checker (its launcher and
PyQt6, and the tools gcc, make, git, kmod, eject and udevadm, new in the catalog), the portal (apps.toml), the
wiki (its chapter, the apps overview and the Home page), the README and CLAUDE.md list it; the portal's tile icon
is a placeholder in the suite's purple until the owner draws it. Decided by the owner on 17-10-2026 after the
driver was proven by hand on the board: the modules live under /var and load with insmod, so no reboot is ever
needed. Open: the board test of the app, the portal/VERSION minor bump for the new card and the first release
(owner). MIGRATION.md says what the next session starts with: the owner's new app icons, then the new quiz
questions for Bazzite DatStation.

Changelog: 17-10-2026 03:18:11

MIGRATION.md: the USB Wi-Fi item (the AIC8800 driver for the UGREEN AX900) is started, with the groundwork of
17-10-2026: Secure Boot is unsupported on the board, Bazzite ships the matching kernel-devel and gcc, and the
radxa-pkg/aic8800 USB driver builds against kernel 7.2.9 without errors; the first load test showed the owner's stick
is the older MCU revision (chip_mcu_id 1), for which shenmintao/aic8800d80's legacy-mcu1 branch carries the matched
firmware; built from that branch, the stick comes up as wlan0, scans both bands and connects on 5 GHz with WPA2 (the
firmware does no WPA3) at 200 Mbit/s. The build kit and the test commands for the owner are in the item. Console
Link's open Wi-Fi test is done with it: 17 minutes of 1080p/60 streams over Wi-Fi, equal to the cable on every
network measure, with one real Wi-Fi hiccup of 3 lost frames that the recovery handled as built (a held picture
for a moment, no smearing), under the Console Link item. No code in the suite changes.

Changelog: 17-10-2026 01:38:16

From a copyright scan of the repository. The Windows zip of an app (tools/build_windows_exe.py) carries
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt: the exe holds Python, Qt and the app's Python packages, whose licenses ask for their notices
to go with it; the file has Python's license, each package the app's requirements pull in with its license files from
the package metadata, and the fonts' license; tests in tools/tests/test_build_windows_exe.py. .gitignore leaves out
/.cache/, the fonts MkDocs' privacy plugin downloads at build time, which had been committed with a release.
MIGRATION.md lists the pictures still to replace.

