Changelog: 16-10-2026 17:13:29

tools/icons/ draws the suite's icon family: one frame per class in tools/icons/frames (the owner's art, 512 px, the
same dark center in each), per app a glowing symbol in the class color in that center. make_icons.py lists each of
the 29 apps with its frame, color, symbol and outputs (none yet: `--sheet PATH` draws them all on one review picture
first). The emulators' labels (PS3, PSP, VITA) are drawn as strokes, not from a font, so they come out the same on
every machine. The portal keeps its purple board icon, which the wiki shows too. tools/tests/test_icon_family.py
checks that every frame has the same center and that each icon is its frame with only the center filled.

Changelog: 16-10-2026 12:10:30

tools/tag-release.sh refuses a portal tag until every app release that HEAD's apps.toml pins is tagged on origin
and pinned with its sha256: the portal-v1.9.0 tag was pushed before vita3k-manager-v0.1.0 existed, and its release
failed on check_manifest.py --require-tags. The message says what comes first (tag the app, then step 2's pin). Its message for a tag that exists already
says that deleting it needs the release-tag ruleset disabled for a moment, as GitHub refuses it otherwise.
Tests: tools/tests/test_tag_release.py; the wiki's portal page says it.

Changelog: 16-10-2026 11:57:04

tools/check_changelogs.py checks that no CHANGELOG loses history: every entry a CHANGELOG had at the base (its
"Changelog: <time>" line) is still in it, so an old entry may be corrected but not dropped, and a CHANGELOG goes only
with its folder. CI runs it against the last push (or the PR base) beside check_manifest.py, and tools/pre-push.sh
runs it before a push. Found when a release push cut the root CHANGELOG and the portal's down to their newest entry
(1017 and 699 lines to 8 and 7); their history was put back. Tests: tools/tests/test_check_changelogs.py, and the
pre-push test calls it. The development chapter of the wiki and CLAUDE.md list it.

Changelog: 16-10-2026 11:32:38

The Development chapter of the wiki describes the Vita3K Manager's pin beside the other upstream pins: where it
is (emulator.py), where a new build's digest and size come from (its Vita3K-builds release), why the Upstream
workflow does not check it (a build almost daily; the app says when one is newer), and what a new pin needs a look
at in Vita3K's source: the command line, the folders and pref-path, the firmware's three parts, the SDL frontend
and --fullscreen, the AppImage's self-updater, and the config.yml fixture of the pinned build.

