Changelog: 15-10-2026 23:22:38

Semantic versioning (owner's decision, 15-10-2026): every new entry in an app's, core's or the portal's CHANGELOG
starts with Breaking., Added. or Fixed. (major, minor, patch), and BC250 Suite Releases offers the version that asks
for (see its CHANGELOG). tools/tests/test_changelog_kinds.py checks the entries from now on; CLAUDE.md and the
wiki's Architecture page have the rule and the table.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 23:13:51

tools/pre-push.sh runs CI's quick checks before a push, in a few seconds: check_versions.py, check_manifest.py
against what the remote has (the check the release push of 15-10-2026 failed on: apps.toml changed without the portal
bump), the exec bits and the line endings of the pushed commit. tools/hooks/pre-push makes it git's pre-push hook
(git config core.hooksPath tools/hooks); BC250_PRE_PUSH=full also runs tools/ci-local.sh, git push --no-verify skips
it. Tests in tools/tests/test_pre_push.py. fix-modes.sh and CI's exec-bit check cover tools/hooks/ too, CI
shellchecks the hook, and the development page of the wiki and CLAUDE.md name it.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 22:22:25

CLAUDE.md has the rule Advice, not reboots (owner, 15-10-2026): no app reboots, powers off or logs out the board; it
says when one is needed. The bisect tools' reboots between rounds (CU Bisect, Cores Bisect, with --auto by themselves)
and Cores Unlock's one warm reboot after a cold boot are the exception, by design. Bazzite Test's leftover --no-prompt
option went (see its CHANGELOG).

Changelog: 15-10-2026 22:11:53

