Changelog: 15-10-2026 22:04:04

Privacy (owner, 15-10-2026: everything about the suite may be public, personal data never). The wiki loads nothing
from other sites any more: Material's privacy plugin (mkdocs.yml) downloads the fonts (Inter, JetBrains Mono, which
came from Google Fonts on every page view, sending each visitor's IP address to Google) and Mermaid (from unpkg) at
build time and serves them from the wiki. A new Privacy page (docs/privacy.md, under Security, and a question on the
Home page) says what the suite sends where and when, app by app, what stays on the board, how logs are masked, what
GitHub Pages sees of a visit, and how to report a privacy problem. CLAUDE.md has the rule (Open by default), and the
scope rule names its one exception: the Dependency Checker shows Bazzite's update state and reminds weekly when an
update waits (see its CHANGELOG).

Changelog: 15-10-2026 21:51:30

A weekly backlog review (owner's request): .github/workflows/backlog.yml runs on Mondays (07:00 UTC, and by hand) and
opens the "Backlog review" issue, or updates the open one with a comment, listing every item MIGRATION.md says is on
hold, by section, each linked to its line (tools/backlog.py). GitHub notifies the owner of the new issue or comment;
closing it after the review lets next week open a new one. With nothing on hold it does nothing. The workflow may only
write issues. CLAUDE.md says how to mark an item on hold. Tests: tools/tests/test_backlog.py.

