The wiki's GitHub settings page (Development) has a section on GitHub's API limit: 60 requests an hour without signing
in, shared per network address, 5,000 signed in, unchanged answers free; how BC250 Suite Releases shows it, that a
used-up limit is nothing to fix, and how to sign in with gh so the app uses that login.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 04:06:38

tools/check_versions.py reads a version copy with a comment after it (__version__ = "x.y.z"  # ...), and a line that
assigns a literal version in another form is an error instead of being skipped. The comment made it skip the copies of
Bazzite NetcatGUI, Bazzite pkgxtractor and Bazzite UMD File Renamer, so Suite Releases' bump, which changes exactly
the copies found there, left them at 0.1.0 while VERSION went to 0.1.1, and their version tests failed in CI. 36
copies are checked now, up from 33. Tests: tools/tests/test_check_versions.py.

